## 5. On the subagent's notification (all foreground)

I check every changed statement against the evidence file, then:

```bash
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
<project docs-only check>; git grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"    # must be empty
git add -A && git commit -m "docs: close WireGuard keepalive relay (PR #165)"   # Co-Authored-By trailer only
git push -u origin chore/wg-keepalive-docs && gh pr create --fill && gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch
```

Write `memory/wg-keepalive-relay.md` (type `project`: the relay mechanism and the traps from my run logs) and add its line to `MEMORY.md`. Then cleanup:

```bash
herdr agent get wgka                                   # idle, focused:false
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain   # must be empty; never --force
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree prune && git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible pull
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
ps -p 48211 -o pid,lstart,command                      # confirm it is my 21:30 broker
kill 48211
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree list
```

Backlog: WG `done`, `docs closed: yes`; republish. I send both product advisors the new `ccs-it.md` SHA, then the next status.

## Why

- **"Accepted" closes stage 12, not the task.** `done` needs docs closed and cleanup (§8). The snapshot is also an input: the product advisors read the repo tonight, and a pre-relay `ccs-it.md` would feed the RDP design stale facts.
- **RDP audio is a new task, so stage 0 comes first** (§10a). The design comes from two product advisors and a 2/2 vote, not from an executor and not from me.
- **`wgka` is not reused.** One tab is one task (§4); its knowledge of the roles does not change that, and an executor may exist only after `brainstormed`.
- **"By morning" is a wish.** It shortens no round. The full brainstorm can plausibly finish overnight, so nothing conflicts with a rule yet and I do not poll. If it cannot finish, that is the operator's poll.
- **Nothing here is a choice.** Every step is decided or routine, and the docs-only merge needs no vote.
- **Both long jobs run in the background**, so I supervise rather than wait.
- **Leftovers are harmless only tonight.** After nine hours, the backlog and memory are what survive my own compaction.
